<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The District strives to balance the operating budget with current revenues, ensuring that current revenues cover ongoing expenditures. Excess fund balance in the general operating fund may be used for one-time, non-recurring expenditures or capital needs. During challenging economic times, and with careful planning and multi-year budgeting, the Board of Trustees may use a portion of the fund balance to offset costs that exceed limited revenues, thereby protecting the integrity of programs and the success of the District without compromising its financial stability.  )
/E (The District strives to balance the operating budget with current revenues, ensuring that current revenues cover ongoing expenditures. Excess fund balance in the general operating fund may be used for one-time, non-recurring expenditures or capital needs. During challenging economic times, and with careful planning and multi-year budgeting, the Board of Trustees may use a portion of the fund balance to offset costs that exceed limited revenues, thereby protecting the integrity of programs and the success of the District without compromising its financial stability.  )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6 7]
